    "result_text": "Green \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nBoth findings were valid and matched the repo's established convention (domain rules live in a `single-source-of-truth` helper; `Normalize*` steps are thin orchestration). I agreed with both.\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 placement of the composition rule.** Moved the \"prefer structured, compose flat\" knowledge out of the step and into `OwnerAddresses`, where the repo documents the normalized-address definition to live:\n- Added `OwnerAddresses.resolve(addressLine1, addressLine2, flatAddress)` returning a small `Normalized(addressLine1, addressLine2, address)` record. It owns the structured-vs-flat preference and the `line1 + \" \" + line2` composition.\n- Updated the `OwnerAddresses` class javadoc so it again accurately describes *the whole* definition (including structured composition) \u2014 fixing the staleness the review flagged.\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress` is now back to the thin \"call helper \u2192 store \u2192 escalate if blank\" shape of its siblings like `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`.\n\n**Finding 2 \u2014 double `line2.isBlank()`.** Resolved as a natural consequence: `hasLine2` is computed once inside `resolve`.\n\nNo behavioural change \u2014 the composition/normalization/validation semantics are identical, just relocated, and the acceptance suite confirms it.",
